# Chat Service — Project Rules

Engineering: `@engineering-principles`. New features: `@feature-pipeline`.

## Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|-------|------------|
| Framework | Django (async views, ASGI) |
| Database | PostgreSQL via Django ORM |
| API | REST + OpenAPI documentation |
| Real-time | WebSockets or SSE (when needed) |
| Tests | pytest + pytest-django |

## Package layout

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `config/` | Project settings, `urls.py`, `asgi.py` |
| `apps/` | Django apps (`accounts`, `chat`, `core`, …) |
| `apps/*/services/` | Business logic |
| `apps/*/views/` or `api/` | HTTP handlers |
| `tests/` | Cross-app integration tests |
| `scripts/` | Deploy, automation |

**Request flow:** HTTP/WS → ASGI → view → service → ORM → PostgreSQL

## Conventions

- Config via env vars and split settings modules; `.env` for local dev (never committed)
- DB: Django migrations; schema `public` in DB `DB_NAME`
- `snake_case` for Python; kebab-case for URL paths
- Pin dependencies in `requirements.txt` or `pyproject.toml`

Shared agent references: `.cursor/agents/shared/`.
